---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import SeparatorDemo from "../../components/SeparatorDemo";
import SeparatorFadeDemo from "../../components/SeparatorFadeDemo";
import SeparatorMarkerDemo from "../../components/SeparatorMarkerDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Separator"
  description="Lines that divide content, label form sections, mark a point in a transcript, and note events in a timeline."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Separator</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A thin line that divides related content. It can be horizontal or vertical,
    carry a centered label, fade toward a transcript label, or become a quiet
    timeline note.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><SeparatorDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Separator usage"
      code={`import { Separator } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/separator";

<p>Project details</p>
<Separator />

<div className="flex items-center gap-3">
  <span>Meadow</span>
  <Separator orientation="vertical" />
  <span>Updated today</span>
</div>

<div role="group" aria-label="Pages" className="flex">
  <Button variant="ghost">Previous</Button>
  <Separator tone="input" orientation="vertical" />
  <Button variant="ghost">Next</Button>
</div>

<Separator>or</Separator>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>orientation</code> is <code>"horizontal"</code> (default) or <code
        >"vertical"</code
      >. A horizontal line fills the width. A vertical line stretches to the
      height of its flex row. <code>tone</code> is <code>"default"</code>, which
      uses <code>--sprout-line</code>, or <code>"input"</code>, which uses <code
        >--sprout-input</code
      > to match control borders inside button groups. In a column of buttons, use
      a horizontal separator.
    </p>
    <p>
      Separator has no margin. Add spacing with <code>className</code>, for
      example <code>my-2</code> between list rows. <code>className</code> may be a
      function of <code>{"{ orientation }"}</code>, and the Base UI <code
        >render</code
      > prop swaps the element.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Variants</h2>
    <p>
      <code>variant</code> and <code>children</code> pick the shape. The root always
      gets <code>data-slot="separator"</code> and a <code>data-variant</code>.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>"line"</code> (default) draws a bare 1px rule in either orientation.
      </li>
      <li>
        A line with <code>children</code> centers short content such as "or". Its
        <code>data-variant</code> is <code>"label"</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>"fade"</code> fades the line toward a centered text label. Use it to
        mark a point in a transcript.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>"marker"</code> is a quiet, full-width timeline note with an icon and
        text.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>"marker-border"</code> adds a line under the marker row. Use it to head
        a group of events.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Labeled separator</h2>
    <p>
      Pass <code>children</code> to center short text such as "or" or a section name
      on a horizontal line. The labeled row takes <code>div</code> props. Children
      that render nothing, such as <code>false</code>, keep the same 20px
      height, so form spacing stays even. Long text stays on one line and ends
      with an ellipsis.
    </p>
    <p>
      Put a <code>SeparatorIcon</code> before the text for an icon and label between
      two lines. Use this to split a timeline by day.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Fade</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Fade usage"
      code={`<Separator variant="fade">Auto compacted</Separator>
<Separator variant="fade">Compacted</Separator>`}
    />
    <p>
      With <code>variant="fade"</code>, <code>children</code> is a required string.
      It is shown between the lines and also names the separator. The fade fills the
      width of its container and has no margin, so add spacing with the parent's <code
        >gap</code
      > or with <code>className</code>. Other
      <code>div</code> props and the Base UI <code>render</code> prop pass through.
    </p>
    <p>
      The lines fade in from the edges toward the label. On hover, a soft
      highlight sweeps across the lines and label once. Long labels stay on one
      line and end with an ellipsis.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6"><SeparatorFadeDemo client:load /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Marker</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Marker usage"
      code={`import {
  Separator,
  SeparatorContent,
  SeparatorIcon,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/separator";
import { BookOpen } from "reicon-react/icons/BookOpen";
import { Calendar } from "reicon-react/icons/Calendar";
import { History } from "reicon-react/icons/History";

<Separator variant="marker">
  <SeparatorIcon><BookOpen size={16} /></SeparatorIcon>
  <SeparatorContent>Used skill Weekly report · 3f9a2c1b</SeparatorContent>
</Separator>

<Separator>
  <SeparatorIcon><Calendar /></SeparatorIcon>
  Today
</Separator>

<Separator variant="marker-border">
  <SeparatorIcon><History /></SeparatorIcon>
  <SeparatorContent>Yesterday · 4 events</SeparatorContent>
</Separator>`}
    />
    <p>
      A marker renders a <code>div</code> with 14px muted text and 8px between its
      parts. <code>"marker-border"</code> adds a 1px line and 8px of space under the
      row. There is one size.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>SeparatorIcon</code> is a 16px slot. An <code>svg</code> inside it is
      16px unless you give it a size class. <code>SeparatorContent</code>
      holds the marker text. Long words wrap, so the row never overflows its column.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6"><SeparatorMarkerDemo client:load /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Marker links</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Links in a marker"
      code={`<Separator variant="marker">
  <SeparatorContent>
    Robin edited the brief · <a href="/changes">View changes</a>
  </SeparatorContent>
</Separator>

<Separator variant="marker" render={<a href="/skills/weekly-report" />}>
  <SeparatorIcon><BookOpen size={16} /></SeparatorIcon>
  <SeparatorContent>Open skill Weekly report</SeparatorContent>
</Separator>`}
    />
    <p>
      A link directly inside <code>SeparatorContent</code> is underlined. So is a
      marker rendered as a link with <code>render</code>. Both turn to the text
      color on hover and keyboard focus and get a focus ring.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Sidebar</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="SidebarSeparator usage"
      code={`import { SidebarSeparator } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/sidebar";

<SidebarGroup>…</SidebarGroup>
<SidebarSeparator />
<SidebarGroup>…</SidebarGroup>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>SidebarSeparator</code> is a Separator inset 8px from each edge, with
      <code>data-sidebar="separator"</code>. <code>SidebarHeader</code> and <code
        >SidebarFooter</code
      > already draw their own border, so use it between groups.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      A line renders <code>role="separator"</code> with <code
        >aria-orientation</code
      >. It is not focusable and does not stop keyboard movement between the
      controls around it. If a line is only decoration, pass <code
        >role="none"</code
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      The text in a labeled separator is read as normal text. The second line is
      hidden from screen readers. <code>SeparatorIcon</code> is <code
        >aria-hidden</code
      >, so put the meaning in words.
    </p>
    <p>
      A fade separator uses its label as its <code>aria-label</code>. The
      highlight copy is hidden from screen readers. The hover sweep only runs on
      devices that can hover, and never when reduced motion is requested.
    </p>
    <p>
      A marker has no role and does not take focus. Screen readers read its
      content as plain text. In forced colors mode the marker border uses the
      system text color.
    </p>
    <p>
      Line and link colors change in 120ms and do not animate when reduced
      motion is requested.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Lines use <code>--sprout-line</code>, and <code>tone="input"</code> uses
      <code>--sprout-input</code>. Labels and marker text use <code
        >--sprout-muted</code
      >. Fade labels are <code>--sprout-text-xs</code>, and the hover highlight
      uses <code>--sprout-text</code>. Hovered and focused marker links use
      <code>--sprout-text</code>, and the focus ring uses <code
        >--sprout-focus</code
      >. Override them in light and dark modes like any other Sprout token.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
